.TH SDL_log10f 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_log10f \- Compute the base-10 logarithm of
.BR x .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "float SDL_log10f(float x);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Domain:
.BR "0 < x <= INF"
.PP
Range:
.BR "-INF <= y <= INF"
.PP
It is an error for
.BR x
to be less than or equal to 0\[char46]
.PP
This function operates on single-precision floating point values, use
.BR SDL_log10
for double-precision floats\[char46]
.PP
This function may use a different approximation across different versions, platforms and configurations\[char46] i\[char46]e, it can return a different value given the same input on different machines or operating systems, or if SDL is updated\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I x
floating point value\[char46] Must be greater than 0\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the logarithm of
.BR x \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_log10 (3),
.BR SDL_logf (3),
.BR SDL_powf (3)
